verses.text:
The mountains shook{b} at the sight of Yahweh,
the God of Sinai,{c}
at the sight of Israel’s God.

“You who ride on pale{h} donkeys,
you who sit on fine rugs,{i}
you who walk along the road,
think about this!{j}

From Ephraim came men whose roots were in Amalek.{m}
Benjamin came behind you with his own people.
From Machir came commanders.
From Zebulun came men who carried the marshal’s staff.{n}

The old river Kishon{r}
washed them all away,
the river Kishon itself.
Go forward, my soul, in strength!{s}
